; =============================================================================
; Float Conversion and Relaxed Float Optimizations for E-Graph
; =============================================================================
;
; This module provides:
; - FP16 (half precision) conversion optimizations
; - FP32/FP64 conversion optimizations
; - Relaxed floating-point optimizations
; - Fast math optimizations
;
; NOTE: FMA rules are in glsl.egg to avoid duplicates.
;
; =============================================================================
; FP16 Conversion Optimization
; =============================================================================
; Converting to half precision and back can often be eliminated.

; Convert to half then back to float = original (with precision loss)
; This is only safe when we don't care about precision
; (ConvertFToHalf x) then (ConvertHToF) could equal x in relaxed mode

; Pack/unpack elimination
(rule ((= e (UnpackHalf2x16 (PackHalf2x16 v))))
      ((union e v)))

; Half precision intermediates that are immediately converted back
; This pattern appears in shaders that compute in half then output float

; =============================================================================
; FP32 <-> FP64 Conversion
; =============================================================================
; Double precision conversion elimination.

; Convert F32 to F64 then back = original (with potential precision loss)
; (FConvert64to32 (FConvert32to64 x)) = x (exact)
; (FConvert32to64 (FConvert64to32 x)) may lose precision - keep as is

; =============================================================================
; Fast Math Optimizations
; =============================================================================
; These assume IEEE non-compliance is acceptable.

; Division by constant can become multiply by reciprocal
; x / c = x * (1/c) when c is constant
; (This is only approximately equal for floats)
; For now, rely on strength reduction rules

; Square root of square = absolute value
; sqrt(x*x) = abs(x) (for real x)
(rule ((= e (Sqrt (FMul x x))))
      ((union e (FAbs x))))

; pow(x, 0.5) = sqrt(x)
; (Already handled in glsl.egg)

; pow(x, 2) = x * x
; (Already handled in glsl.egg)

; =============================================================================
; NaN/Inf Handling
; =============================================================================
; Special handling for NaN and infinity.

; NaN-safe min/max (NMin, NMax are in datatypes.egg)
; These ignore NaN values

; IsNan/IsInf simplification
; IsNan(constant) = false for non-NaN constant
; IsInf(constant) = false for finite constant

; =============================================================================
; Denormal Handling
; =============================================================================
; Denormal (subnormal) float handling.
; Some hardware flushes denormals to zero (FTZ).
; In FTZ mode, very small values become zero.

; For robustness, we don't assume FTZ behavior in the e-graph.
; The driver/runtime handles this.

; =============================================================================
; Precision-Preserving Transformations
; =============================================================================
; These transformations preserve or improve precision.

; Kahan summation pattern recognition
; (Would require multi-statement patterns - complex)

; Compensated summation: track error term
; (Complex - not currently modeled)

; =============================================================================
; Mixed Precision Optimization
; =============================================================================
; Optimize computation across different precisions.

; FP16 arithmetic with FP32 accumulator pattern
; sum = sum + (half)a * (half)b
; Can be: sum = fma((float)(half)a, (float)(half)b, sum)

; =============================================================================
; IsNan/IsInf rules are already in glsl.egg
; =============================================================================
; NOTE: IsNan/IsInf optimization rules are defined in glsl.egg to avoid
; duplication. See glsl.egg for:
; - IsNan(ConvertSToF(x)) = 0
; - IsNan(ConvertUToF(x)) = 0
; - IsInf variants
; - FAbs/FNeg preservation

